Models and data
================================================================================

BirdNET
    https://birdnet.cornell.edu
    K. Lisa Yang Center for Conservation Bioacoustics at the Cornell Lab of
    Ornithology, and Chemnitz University of Technology.
    Provides the acoustic models that identify species, the GeoModel location
    filter, and the taxonomy.

    The BirdNET models are licensed under Creative Commons
    Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0):
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

    NON-COMMERCIAL USE ONLY. Because the models carry a non-commercial licence,
    no distribution of this project as a whole may be put to commercial use,
    whatever the licence on the source code itself.

eBird Status and Trends
    https://science.ebird.org/en/status-and-trends
    Cornell Lab of Ornithology.
    Provides the weekly occurrence data behind the seasonality timeline and the
    source data for the range maps.

    Access and redistribution are governed by the eBird Status and Trends
    Products Terms of Use. Anyone redistributing derived products (for example
    the region packs this project builds) must confirm their own permission
    under those terms.

xeno-canto
    https://xeno-canto.org
    Reference recordings shown on species pages. Individual recordings are
    licensed by their contributors, most under Creative Commons licences that
    require attribution to the recordist.


